#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installing &kdevelop;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>installation</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this chapter we will discuss the steps necessary to compile and install "
"the &kdevelop; IDE:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"kdevelop-install-howto\">How to obtain &kdevelop;</link> "
"mainly concentrates on downloading the most recent &kdevelop; sources from "
"CVS."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"requirements\">&kdevelop; requirements</link> lists the "
"programs and libraries which you need installed to successfully compile the "
"IDE."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"compile-and-install\">&kdevelop; compilation and "
"installation</link> leads you through all the steps of compilation and "
"installation of the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"make-api\">How to obtain a &kdevelop; &API; documentation</"
"link> tells what an API is and how you get such a useful tool for navigating "
"the &kdevelop; sources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Obtain &kdevelop;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "obtain &kdevelop;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:40 kdevelop-install.docbook:65
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:119 kdevelop-install.docbook:166
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:342 kdevelop-install.docbook:345
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:599 kdevelop-install.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>&kdevelop;</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "obtain"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; is available in binary form from many different &Linux; "
"distributions such as SuSE, RedHat and others. These binaries are packed in "
"some convenient format, mostly RPM, for easy installation. To install, "
"follow the standard instructions given in your distribution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may as well obtain the &kdevelop; sources, compile and install them by "
"yourself. These sources can be found via the project home page at <ulink url="
"\"http://www.kdevelop.org\"> http://www.kdevelop.org</ulink> or via the "
"<ulink url=\"http://download.kde.org\">&kde; ftp site</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "Get Daily &kdevelop; Snapshots from &CVS;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:54 kdevelop-install.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>CVS</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want be in front of current development, anonymous &CVS; repository "
"snapshots are available. The module name is <emphasis>kdevelop</emphasis> at "
"<filename class=\"directory\">:pserver:anonymous@anoncvs.kde.org:/home/kde</"
"filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Initial &CVS; Checkout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>checkout</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:66 kdevelop-install.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>CVS</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: tertiary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "<tertiary>checkout</tertiary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To obtain an initial version of &kdevelop; you must download it from "
"anonymous &CVS;. For this so-called <emphasis>checkout</emphasis> operation "
"follow these steps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We assume you want to put your &kdevelop; copy into the <filename class="
"\"directory\">kde3src</filename> subdirectory of your home directory "
"(<filename class=\"directory\">~</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "# Create the destination directory, if necessary:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~&gt; </prompt> <userinput>mkdir kde3src</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:85 kdevelop-install.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~&gt; </prompt> <userinput>cd kde3src</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src&gt; </prompt> <userinput>cvs -z3 -d :pserver:"
"anonymous@anoncvs.kde.org:/home/kde co kdevelop</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:93 kdevelop-install.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~/kde3src&gt; </prompt> <userinput>cd kdevelop</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have successfully checked out your &kdevelop; version, you may keep "
"up with the changes using the update procedure shown in the next section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep the server load low. <emphasis>Please do not checkout every time you "
"want to keep your &kdevelop; up to date!</emphasis> Use CVS update for this "
"purpose."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you may compile your &kdevelop; version as shown in the <link linkend="
"\"compile-and-install\">&kdevelop; Compilation and Installation</link> "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keeping Your &CVS; Copy up to Date"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>update</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: tertiary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "<tertiary>update</tertiary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you checked out (and successfully compiled) &kdevelop; from CVS as "
"shown above, you'll want to keep it up to date in order to get all the "
"patches. Follow these steps. (We again assume you have put your &kdevelop; "
"copy into the <filename class=\"directory\">kde3src</filename> directory.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note the <command>up</command> (= <emphasis>update</emphasis>) command "
"instead of the <command>co</command> (which stands for <emphasis>checkout</"
"emphasis>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src&gt; </prompt> <userinput>cvs -z3 -d :pserver:"
"anonymous@anoncvs.kde.org:/home/kde up kdevelop</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep an eye on the messages &CVS; produces during the update sequence. The "
"exact steps in the compilation sequence depend on this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can compile a new &kdevelop; version as shown in the <link linkend="
"\"compile-and-install-make-cvs\">Special &CVS; compilation considerations</"
"link> chapter."
msgstr ""

