#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case you use a &kdevelop; snapshot from &CVS; the initial compilation "
"steps depend on whether you just did a complete checkout or only updated the "
"source."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "After a CVS Checkout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must <emphasis>initialize the make system</emphasis> after a fresh "
"checkout. The same is true every time you need to start over from scratch. "
"Type:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>make -f admin/Makefile."
"common cvs-clean</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "and then <emphasis>all of the following steps</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You might need access to the &CVS; repository for the clean-up if any "
"corrupted or missing files must be reconstructed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>cvs-clean</command> command will <emphasis>remove every file</"
"emphasis> not in &CVS; from the directory! Make sure to back up any valuable "
"information before you issue this clean-up command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid "After a CVS Update"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next step depends on the output of the &CVS; update sequence. If you got "
"something like (there may be a U or a P marker in the leftmost column, both "
"denoting the file has been changed):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:478
#, no-c-format
msgid "U /some_directory_path/Makefile.am"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "or if you just did a full checkout, you must enter:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>make -f Makefile.cvs</"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"before you proceed with <emphasis>all of the following steps</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic <command>make</command> Command Sequence"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the basic make system is set up you must decide which type of the "
"&kdevelop; system you want to use. This is done in the following configure "
"step which builds the actual <filename>Makefile</filename>s the "
"<command>make</command> command will use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:501
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may drop the <option>--prefix</option> option in the following "
"<command>configure</command> command lines if you want &kdevelop; be "
"installed in the default &kde; directory. See the <link linkend=\"compile-"
"and-install-options\">Some notes on configure options</link> chapter for "
"this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Debug-Compiled Version"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to keep track of what your &kdevelop; application does at run-"
"time you may build a debug-compiled version. Just command "
"<command>configure</command> to do so:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>./configure --enable-"
"debug=full --prefix=</userinput>(where-your-kde3-is)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Release-Compiled Version"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you only want to use &kdevelop; as-is a (smaller and faster running) "
"release version suffices. <command>configure</command> defaults to this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:527 kdevelop-install.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>./configure --prefix=</"
"userinput>(where-your-kde3-is)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to build your own <link linkend=\"make-api\">API documentation</"
"link> for &kdevelop; you must include yet another option in the "
"<command>configure</command> command:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>./configure --</"
"userinput>(options-as-above) <userinput>\\</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:538 kdevelop-install.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid "--with-kdelibsdoxy-dir=$KDEDIR/share/doc/HTML/en/kdelibs-apidocs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make and Install &kdevelop;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>configure</command> will check the system and build some "
"<filename>Makefile</filename>s according to what it found. The "
"<command>make</command> command will use the main <filename>Makefile</"
"filename> by default. Thus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "suffices. If necessary, now gain root user rights using the command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:558 kdevelop-install.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>su</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid "and entering the root password. Then install the application:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"That's all. If you installed &kdevelop; in the default &kde; directory you "
"may now run the IDE. Otherwise some additional steps will be necessary as "
"shown in the <link linkend=\"compile-and-install-options-dir\">Non-default "
"installation directory</link> section below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In fact there usually will have been three &kdevelop;-based applications "
"installed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kdevelop; IDE &mdash; this is the place where you will usually work."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The stand-alone &kdevelop; Assistant documentation browser &mdash; isolates "
"all the powerful documentation facilities of the &kdevelop; IDE in a "
"separate tool. This comes in handy when you want to look up some programming "
"documentation but do not want to start the full IDE."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kdevelop; Designer &mdash; enhances the &Qt; User Interface Designer by "
"&kde; specific elements and integrates nicely in the &kdevelop; IDE."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some Notes on <command>configure</command> Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid "Non-default Installation Directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: tertiary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "<tertiary>non-default directory</tertiary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>non-default directory</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEDIRS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "kbuildsycoca"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default <command>configure</command> prepares the IDE to be installed in "
"the default &kde; directory. This is necessary because &kdevelop; assumes "
"direct access to some tools and parts which reside there. If want to use "
"your own installation directory, you must tell <command>configure</command> "
"this by the <option>--prefix</option> option:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a caveat if you do so. You must provide a means for &kdevelop; to "
"access the needed tools and parts in the &kde; directory when running. (You "
"can still use the IDE without doing so, but with very restrained "
"capabilities.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Call up a shell and have the following commands executed before you start "
"&kdevelop; at the shell prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Take care to use the plural:</emphasis> It is "
"<quote><envar>KDEDIRS</envar></quote>, not just <quote><envar>KDEDIR</"
"envar></quote>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~&gt; </prompt> <userinput>export KDEDIRS=/usr/local/kde:/opt/kde3</"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~&gt; </prompt> <userinput>kbuildsycoca</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "(Now start &kdevelop;:)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>~&gt; </prompt> <userinput>kdevelop</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> environment variable must be set to the "
"<emphasis>list of active &kde; directories</emphasis> in your system. We use"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr/local/kde</filename>:<filename class="
"\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid "as an example only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/local/kde</filename> directory may "
"for instance contain an incomplete &kde; version you compiled for debug "
"purposes, and the <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename> "
"directory may in addition contain the standard &kde; version from your "
"distribution that is used for everyday work."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid "In a tcsh shell you must set the environment variables using:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~&gt; </prompt> <userinput>setenv KDEDIRS /usr/local/kde:/opt/kde3</"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:659
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>kbuildsycoca</command> command (<quote>build system control "
"cache</quote>) looks around for libraries and caches their location and "
"version, so that &kdevelop; can find them. The caveat is that it takes "
"noticeable time&mdash;and it has to be run any time you call up the shell to "
"start &kdevelop; from a non-default directory. You may want to put the above "
"commands into a shell script to reduce the typing effort."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(You could as well put the lines in your <filename>.bashrc</filename> or "
"<filename>.cshrc</filename> file, but this is not advisable as "
"<command>kbuildsycoca</command> will then be run any time you call up the "
"shell.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>kbuildsycoca</command> command does not run from within the "
"root. You must call it from a non-root user. (But is <emphasis>not a very "
"good idea</emphasis> after all to do software development from within the "
"root!)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:678
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Obtain a &kdevelop; API Documentation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:681
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>API</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>API</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: tertiary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid "<tertiary>API</tertiary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "configure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdevelop; API"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"API is the short form of <quote>Application Program Interface</quote>. "
"Actually such an API cotains a series of descriptions (&ie; calling "
"conventions) by which an application program can access the operating system "
"and other services. In our context, however, a broader definition was "
"adopted. The API of a &kde; or &Qt; application is an abstract of the "
"classes and methods interfaces, a synopsis to be used like a dictionary to "
"navigate the sources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:697
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a version of the most current API available at the <ulink url="
"\"http://www.kdevelop.org/HEAD/doc/api/html/index.html\">KDevelop-Home "
"website</ulink>. It will be automatically updated every 24 hours so you can "
"keep up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:700
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alas, this version is best used read-only over the internet. If you do not "
"always have internet access you may as well build your own API documentation "
"from the &kdevelop; sources. To do so, you must tell the automake system "
"where to find the KDELIBS API in your system. This is accomplished by the "
"special option <option>--with-kdelibsdoxy-dir</option> in the "
"<command>configure</command> command when you prepare to compile the "
"&kdevelop; sources:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>./configure --</"
"userinput>(options-as-usual)<userinput> \\</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(<command>make</command> will replace the global <varname>$KDEDIR</varname> "
"variable with the actual &kde; directory setting recorded therein.) Then "
"issue a <command>make</command> command <link linkend=\"compile-and-install-"
"make-basic\">as usual</link>. After the &kdevelop; IDE has been built you "
"have the option to build the API as well. For this you must issue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>make apidocs</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will build a <filename>Doxyfile</filename> in your &kdevelop; base "
"directory which in turn will be processed by the <application>Doxygen</"
"application> application to build quite a lot of <filename>.html</filename> "
"API files. When this rather lengthy API building process (may last more than "
"an hour on a slow system) finally comes to an end, you must install the API "
"just like you have to install the &kdevelop; IDE itself. If necessary obtain "
"superuser rights by"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid "and entering the root password. Then install the API files:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>~/kde3src/kdevelop&gt; </prompt> <userinput>make install-apidox</"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:740
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once this is done, <command>make</command> will inform you about the "
"directory where you can finally look at the API documentation's contents. "
"Note this address, you can use it from &konqueror; as well as from inside "
"&kdevelop;, in case you have set up the &kdevelop; sources themselves as a "
"project to work on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-install.docbook:744
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will most probably see a lot of warning and/or error messages during the "
"API build run by <application>Doxygen</application>. It is best to ignore "
"them, they are of interest to the &kdevelop; developers only. If the API "
"generation ever comes to a successful end, the <filename>.html</filename> "
"API files will be usable."
msgstr ""
